        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5aeea2a9-f25e-5cd8-82e8-26e35cb783ef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sanming, Jiutai District, Datian County, Yinma River, western Fujian, Jilin, Changchun, Yitong Manchu Autonomous County, Panshi, Dehui, Nong'an County, Kaoshan, Second Songhua River\n- Topics: Administrative divisions, River geography\n\nFacts:\n- Sanming is a prefecture-level city in western Fujian province, China.\n- Jiutai District is a district under the jurisdiction of Changchun, the capital of Jilin province, China.\n- Datian County is under the jurisdiction of Sanming City.\n- The Yinma River originates in Yitong Manchu Autonomous County.\n- The Yinma River flows generally from south to north across Panshi, Jiutai, and Dehui.\n- The Yinma River joins the Second Songhua River at Kaoshan in Nong'an County.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
